  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), STECS Mini Plus with left Space Throttle Grip (STECS-MiniP-STG-L_04) seen from the right front and above: grip thumb face, pointer stalk, base panel and the ATEM module in front (ARMED, 1-4, PUSH, SAFE all labelled)",
  "mappingSource": "catalog vkb.json: EDCD community map 231D0137 (https://github.com/EDCD/EliteCustomButtonNames/blob/main/files/INTO%20Bindings/DeviceButtonMaps/231D0137.buttonMap, factory profile); grip control names and spots from VKB's STECS Space Throttle LH template v1.0 (https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0808/7827/2731/files/VKB-STECS-SpaceThrottleGrip-LH-v1.0.pdf; leader lines on a photo of nearly this angle) and ATEM template v1.0 (https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0808/7827/2731/files/VKB-STECS-ATEM-v1.0.pdf), both linked on https://vkbsimcontrollers.com/pages/downloads; printed labels (H1, HAT1, B1, B2, SPEED LIM, H2, ARMED, 1-4, PUSH, SAFE)",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "gallery-2, 3, 8, 9, 10 (STECS-MiniP-STG-R_*) show the RIGHT-hand grip, another product. hat.3 = H1 (3-way up/down/push), hat.4 = H2 (push + left/right in the template) as in the STG Standard draft. The main trigger is on the hidden front of the grip. The grip X/Y gimbal (template STG x/y) has no catalog part. ATEM SAFE/ARMED is one catalog part (toggle.5: BTN10 SAFE = up, BTN15 ARMED = down); the marker sits on SAFE, ARMED is the pad at 0.255 0.643. MODE 1-5 are the positions of the white rotary.",
